<blockquote class="uncited"><div>Hello everyone,<br><br>I would like to use a global variable that would be visible in all the code, do you know in which file I should define my variable?<br><br>JP7NJT</div></blockquote>The code is partially modular and you don't normally expect to have variables that every single function has access to.<br><br>Most variables are declared as static to individual files, to deliberately limit their scope.<br><br>This is normal / good programming practice, to limit variability scope.<br><br>If you need a variable that is visible to every function, you will probably need to making a new .c file and a new .h and then include that new .h in every file that needs access to your 'global' variable<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Fri Dec 08, 2023 2:02 am</p><hr />
